IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`

-- coa-proc-scheme-of-arrangement.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 26, ss 895 to 901: the procedure the Act lays down for a
-- compromise or arrangement with creditors or members, written as regulative rules over the Boolean encoding in coa20-part26.l4.
-- Lines 12205-12331 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- The gates are the existing functions of coa20-part26.l4 (s 895(1), s 896(1) and (2), s 897(4), s 897(5), s 898, s 899(1), (2) and s 899A(5), s 900(1) and (7),
-- s 901(1), (3)); the majority of s 899(1) is counted there, from the numbers present and voting and the numbers who agree.
-- Nothing here edits that module, and nothing here calls its DEONTIC for s 900(6).
-- The functions of coa20-part26.l4 that answer "was it complied with?" (s 897(1), s 900(6) in time, s 901(2)) are not used as gates: the trace says what was done.
--
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS: the court's outcome (an order made, a sanction given); that a meeting is summoned; that a notice is given by advertisement;
-- that the person has applied in the manner the notice indicates (s 897(4)); the officer is in default (s 1121); the defence of s 897(7) is shown;
-- that the order amends the articles (s 901(2)).
-- NOT ENCODED as acts: s 895(2) and (3) and s 896(3) and (4) (definitions and signposts, Boolean only); s 899(3) (the arrangement binds: an effect, not an act);
-- s 899A(3) and (4) (relevant creditors do not take part in the meeting and are sent the statement); s 900(2) to (5) (what the court may provide, and the
-- vesting of property by the order); the penalties of s 897(8), s 898(3), s 900(8) and s 901(6).

DECLARE `ss 895-901 party` IS ONE OF
    `ss 895-901 the court`
    `ss 895-901 the company`
    `ss 895-901 a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting`
    `ss 895-901 a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders`
    `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default`

DECLARE `ss 895-901 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 896(1) the court orders a meeting to be summoned`
    `s 897(1)(a) the company sends the notice summoning the meeting accompanied by the statement`
    `s 897(1)(b)(i) the company includes the statement in the advertisement`
    `s 897(1)(b)(ii) the company states in the advertisement where and how copies of the statement may be obtained`
    `s 897(4) the creditor or member applies for a copy of the statement`
    `s 897(4) the company provides the copy of the statement free of charge`
    `s 897(5) the company makes default in complying with a requirement of section 897`
    `s 897(5) the officer is in default in the company's default`
    `s 898(1) the director or trustee gives the company notice of the matters relating to himself`
    `s 898(2) the director or trustee makes default in complying with section 898`
    `s 899(1) the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement`
    `s 899(4) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar`
    `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar`
    `s 901(2) the company delivers the amended articles, resolution or agreement with the copy of the order`
    `s 901(3) the company issues a copy of the articles unaccompanied by a copy of the order`

-- ---- s 896: the court orders a meeting -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:12216 | 896 Court order for holding of meeting
-- src:12217 | (1) The court may, on an application under this section, order a meeting of the creditors or class of creditors, or of the members of the company or class of members (as the case may be), to be summoned in such manner as the court directs.
-- src:12218 | (2) An application under this section may be made by—
-- src:12219 | (a) the company,
-- src:12220 | (b) any creditor or member of the company,
-- src:12221 | (c) if the company is being wound up, the liquidator, or
-- src:12222 | (d) if the company is in administration, the administrator.
@ref s 896(1)-(2) Court order for holding of meeting (src:12216-12222)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 896 gives the court no time to order the meeting and the applicant no time to apply, so no clock is encoded: the power stays open until the trace shows it used)
-- FORK: s 896(1) "may" | the court's order is a power (MAY) of the court, gated by the existing functions on the Part applying, an application being made and the applicant being one the subsection lists | the court is bound to order the meeting once asked
GIVEN `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its members, or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application under section 896 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A `s 896(2) applicant`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 896(1) the court's power to order a meeting` MEANS
    IF     (`s 895(1) the provisions of Part 26 apply` `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its creditors, or any class of them` `a compromise or arrangement is proposed between the company and its members, or any class of them`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`s 896(1) the court may order a meeting of the creditors, class of creditors, members or class of members` `an application under section 896 has been made`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`s 896(2) the person may apply for an order for a meeting` applicant `the company is being wound up` `the company is in administration`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the court`
         MAY `s 896(1) the court orders a meeting to be summoned`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 897: the statement sent with the notice ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:12225 | 897 Statement to be circulated or made available
-- src:12226 | (1) Where a meeting is summoned under section 896—
-- src:12227 | (a) every notice summoning the meeting that is sent to a creditor or member must be accompanied by a statement complying with this section, and
-- src:12228 | (b) every notice summoning the meeting that is given by advertisement must either—
-- src:12229 | (i) include such a statement, or
-- src:12230 | (ii) state where and how creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting may obtain copies of such a statement.
@ref s 897(1) Statement to be circulated or made available: the notice (src:12225-12230)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 897(1) ties the statement to the notice and to nothing else: "every notice summoning the meeting that is sent ... must be accompanied", so no clock is encoded and the duty stays owed until the trace shows the notice sent with the statement)
-- FORK: s 897(1)(b) "either (i) include such a statement, or (ii) state where and how" | the two ways of advertising are alternatives (ROR): either one meets the duty | the company must do both
-- FORK: s 897(1) the trigger | "Where a meeting is summoned under section 896" is an input (the court's order of s 896(1) is not the trace's concern); the existing s 897(1) function answers whether the duty was met, so it is not used as the gate | the gate is the existing function
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 896` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `s 897(1) how a notice summoning the meeting is given`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 897(1) the company's duty to send the statement with the notice or make it available` MEANS
    IF `a meeting is summoned under section 896`
    THEN (CONSIDER how
          WHEN `s 897(1) sent to a creditor or member` THEN
              PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
              MUST `s 897(1)(a) the company sends the notice summoning the meeting accompanied by the statement`
              HENCE FULFILLED
          WHEN `s 897(1) given by advertisement` THEN
              (   PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
                  MUST `s 897(1)(b)(i) the company includes the statement in the advertisement`
                  HENCE FULFILLED)
              ROR
              (   PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
                  MUST `s 897(1)(b)(ii) the company states in the advertisement where and how copies of the statement may be obtained`
                  HENCE FULFILLED))
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:12237 | (4) Where a notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting, every such creditor or member is entitled, on making application in the manner indicated by the notice, to be provided by the company with a copy of the statement free of charge.
@ref s 897(4) A copy of the statement free of charge (src:12237-12237)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 897(4) gives the person no time to apply and the company no time to provide the copy, so no clock is encoded: the copy stays owed once the application is made)
-- FORK: s 897(4) "entitled, on making application" | the application is a power (MAY) of the creditor or member, and the company's duty to provide the copy free of charge is the next step after it; the gate is the existing s 897(4) function asked with the application assumed made | the entitlement arises without any application
GIVEN `the notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 897(4) the company's duty to provide a copy of the statement free of charge` MEANS
    IF (`s 897(4) the person is entitled to be provided by the company with a copy of the statement free of charge` `the notice given by advertisement states that copies of an explanatory statement can be obtained by creditors or members entitled to attend the meeting` `the person is a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 a creditor or member entitled to attend the meeting`
         MAY `s 897(4) the creditor or member applies for a copy of the statement`
         HENCE (PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
                MUST `s 897(4) the company provides the copy of the statement free of charge`
                HENCE FULFILLED)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:12238 | (5) If a company makes default in complying with any requirement of this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:12239 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12240 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:12241 | This is subject to subsection (7) below.
-- src:12242 | (6) For this purpose the following are treated as officers of the company—
-- src:12243 | (a) a liquidator or administrator of the company, and
-- src:12244 | (b) a trustee of a deed for securing the issue of debentures of the company.
-- src:12245 | (7) A person is not guilty of an offence under this section if he shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests.
@ref s 897(5)-(7) Offence by the company and every officer in default; the defence (src:12238-12245)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 897(5) says "makes default" and gives no day on which a default is made, so no clock is encoded and the default is an event the trace supplies)
-- FORK: s 897(5) "makes default" | the offence is encoded as a prohibition on the event "makes default in complying with a requirement of section 897" (the company) and on "is in default" (the officer) | the missed notice or statement is itself the default and has a deadline
-- FORK: s 897(5)(b) "every officer of the company who is in default" | a second prohibition on the officer, standing beside the company's (RAND), gated by the existing function with the officer's default (s 1121) as an input; a person treated as an officer by s 897(6) is the officer here | the officer's liability is only a consequence of the company's breach
-- FORK: s 897(7) "if he shows" | each person's defence is its own input and removes that person's prohibition (the existing s 897(5) function does the same) | the defence is shown once for all persons
GIVEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 897(5) the company and every officer in default` MEANS
        (IF (`s 897(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 897` TRUE `s 897(5) the company` (JUST TRUE) `the company shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
              SHANT `s 897(5) the company makes default in complying with a requirement of section 897`
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `ss 895-901 the company` BECAUSE "the company made default in complying with a requirement of section 897: an offence under s 897(5)(a)"
         ELSE FULFILLED)
    RAND
        (IF (`s 897(5) the person is guilty of an offence under section 897` TRUE `s 897(5) an officer of the company` `s 1121 the officer is in default` `the officer shows that the default was due to the refusal of a director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars of his interests`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default`
              SHANT `s 897(5) the officer is in default in the company's default`
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default` BECAUSE "the officer was in default in the company's default under section 897: an offence under s 897(5)(b)"
         ELSE FULFILLED)

-- ---- s 898: the duty of directors and trustees to give information ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:12249 | 898 Duty of directors and trustees to provide information
-- src:12250 | (1) It is the duty of—
-- src:12251 | (a) any director of the company, and
-- src:12252 | (b) any trustee for its debenture holders,
-- src:12253 | to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as may be necessary for the purposes of section 897 (explanatory statement to be circulated or made available).
@ref s 898(1) Duty of directors and trustees to provide information: the duty (src:12249-12253)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 898(1) gives the director or trustee no time to give the notice, so no clock is encoded: the notice stays owed until the trace shows it given)
-- FORK: s 898(1) "such matters relating to himself as may be necessary" | whether a matter is necessary for s 897 is an input, and the director or trustee is the party whichever of the two he is | the duty arises only when the company asks
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of section 897` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 898(1) the duty of a director or trustee to give the company notice` MEANS
    IF (`s 898(1) the person is under a duty to give the company notice of the matter` `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of section 897`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders`
         MUST `s 898(1) the director or trustee gives the company notice of the matters relating to himself`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:12254 | (2) Any person who makes default in complying with this section commits an offence.
-- src:12255 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 898(2) Offence of default (src:12254-12255)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 898(2) says "makes default" and gives no day on which a default is made, so no clock is encoded and the default is an event the trace supplies)
-- FORK: s 898(2) "makes default in complying" | encoded as a prohibition on the event of making default, under the same gate as the duty above | the missed notice is itself the default
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of section 897` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 898(2) the director's or trustee's duty not to make default` MEANS
    IF     (`s 898(1) the person is under a duty to give the company notice of the matter` `the person is a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of section 897`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`s 898(2) the person commits an offence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders`
         SHANT `s 898(2) the director or trustee makes default in complying with section 898`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 895-901 a director of the company or a trustee for its debenture holders` BECAUSE "the director or trustee made default in complying with section 898: an offence under s 898(2)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 899: the court sanctions ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:12257 | 899 Court sanction for compromise or arrangement
-- src:12258 | (1) If a majority in number representing 75% in value of the creditors or class of creditors or members or class of members (as the case may be), present and voting either in person or by proxy at the meeting summoned under section 896, agree a compromise or arrangement, the court may, on an application under this section, sanction the compromise or arrangement.
-- src:12260 | (2) An application under this section may be made by—
-- src:12261 | (a) the company,
-- src:12262 | (b) any creditor or member of the company,
-- src:12263 | (c) if the company is being wound up or an administration order is in force in relation it, the liquidator or administrator.
@ref s 899(1)-(2) Court sanction for compromise or arrangement (src:12257-12263)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 899 gives the court no time to sanction and the applicant no time to apply, so no clock is encoded: the power stays open until the trace shows it used)
-- FORK: s 899(1) "may" | the sanction is a power (MAY) of the court, gated by the existing functions on the majority (a majority in number representing 75% in value of those present and voting), on who may apply, and on s 899A(5) not barring it; the numbers are inputs | the court is bound to sanction once the majority is shown
-- FORK: s 899A(5) | a sanction barred by s 899A(5) (JUST FALSE from the existing function) closes the gate; an answer of NOTHING (s 899A does not apply) leaves it open | any answer but JUST TRUE closes the gate
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 896(2) applicant`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration or an administration order is in force in relation to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application under section 899 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of creditors or members present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 896` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those present and voting` IS A NUMBER
      `the value represented by those who agree` IS A NUMBER
      `s 899A(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the compromise or arrangement includes provision in respect of a relevant creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that relevant creditor has agreed to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 899(1) the court's power to sanction the compromise or arrangement` MEANS
    IF     (`s 899(1) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement` `an application under section 899 has been made` `the number of creditors or members present and voting at the meeting summoned under section 896` `the number of them who agree the compromise or arrangement` `the value represented by those present and voting` `the value represented by those who agree`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`s 899(2) the person may apply for the court's sanction` applicant `the company is being wound up` `the company is in administration or an administration order is in force in relation to it`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (NOT ((`s 899A(5) the court may sanction the compromise or arrangement under section 899` `s 899A(1) this section applies` `the compromise or arrangement includes provision in respect of a relevant creditor` `that relevant creditor has agreed to it`) EQUALS JUST FALSE))
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the court`
         MAY `s 899(1) the court sanctions the compromise or arrangement`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:12269 | (4) The court's order has no effect until a copy of it has been delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 899(4) The order has no effect until a copy is delivered to the registrar (src:12269-12269)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 899(4) names no person who must deliver the copy and gives no time: it says only that the order "has no effect until" delivery, so no clock is encoded; the seven days of s 900(6) belong to an order under s 900 and do not run here)
-- FORK: s 899(4) the delivery | the company's delivery is a power (MAY) it uses to give the order effect: the text states a condition of effect and does not say anyone must deliver | the company must deliver (MUST), with no time
GIVEN `the court has sanctioned the compromise or arrangement by an order under section 899` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 899(4) the company's delivery of a copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the court has sanctioned the compromise or arrangement by an order under section 899`
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
         MAY `s 899(4) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 900: the order facilitating a reconstruction; delivery within seven days ----------------------------------------------

-- src:12292 | 900 Powers of court to facilitate reconstruction or amalgamation
-- src:12293 | (1) This section applies where application is made to the court under section 899 to sanction a compromise or arrangement and it is shown that—
-- src:12294 | (a) the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies, and
-- src:12295 | (b) under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme (“a transferor company”) is to be transferred to another company (“the transferee company”).
-- src:12310 | (6) Every company in relation to which an order is made under this section must cause a copy of the order to be delivered to the registrar within seven days after its making.
@ref s 900(1), (6) Powers of court to facilitate reconstruction or amalgamation: the copy of the order to the registrar (src:12292-12310)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the order under section 900 is made; counting="within seven days after its making" (the Act counts from the making of the order and does not say whether the day of the order is counted, so day 0 is the day of the order and day 7 is the seventh day after it)
-- FORK: s 900(6) "within seven days after its making" | the last day is day 7, the seventh day after the day of the order | the day of the order counts as day 1 and the last day is day 6
-- FORK: s 900(6) "every company in relation to which an order is made" | each such company has its own duty, so the rule is run once for each company, each with its own day 0 (the day the order is made is the same for all) | one company, the transferee, delivers for all
GIVEN `application is made to the court under section 899 to sanction a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme is to be transferred to another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made under section 900` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 900(6) the duty of a company to see that a copy of the order reaches the registrar` MEANS
    IF     (`s 900(1) this section applies` `application is made to the court under section 899 to sanction a compromise or arrangement` `the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies` `under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme is to be transferred to another company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `an order is made under section 900`
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
         MUST `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar`
         WITHIN 7
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 895-901 the company` BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not delivered to the registrar within seven days after its making (s 900(6)): an offence under s 900(7)(a)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:12311 | (7) If default is made in complying with subsection (6) an offence is committed by—
-- src:12312 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12313 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 900(7) Offence of default: the company and every officer in default (src:12311-12313)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the order under section 900 is made; counting="within seven days after its making" (as for the rule above: the default is the missed seventh day, and the offence of the officer follows the company's)
-- FORK: s 900(7)(b) "every officer of the company who is in default" | the officer's liability is the same duty of the company with the breach laid on the officer (RAND beside the company's), gated by the officer's default (s 1121) as an input | a second prohibition on the officer that no time limit drives
GIVEN `application is made to the court under section 899 to sanction a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme is to be transferred to another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made under section 900` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 900(7) the company and every officer in default` MEANS
        (`s 900(6) the duty of a company to see that a copy of the order reaches the registrar` `application is made to the court under section 899 to sanction a compromise or arrangement` `the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies` `under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme is to be transferred to another company` `an order is made under section 900`)
    RAND
        (IF     (`s 900(1) this section applies` `application is made to the court under section 899 to sanction a compromise or arrangement` `the compromise or arrangement is proposed for the purposes of, or in connection with, a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies, or the amalgamation of any two or more companies` `under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme is to be transferred to another company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `an order is made under section 900`
            AND (`s 900(7) the person is guilty of an offence under section 900(7)` TRUE `s 897(5) an officer of the company` `s 1121 the officer is in default`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
              MUST `s 900(6) the company delivers a copy of the order to the registrar`
              WITHIN 7
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `ss 895-901 an officer of the company who is in default` BECAUSE "the officer was in default when a copy of the order was not delivered to the registrar within seven days after its making: an offence under s 900(7)(b)"
         ELSE FULFILLED)

-- ---- s 901: the articles and the order -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:12316 | 901 Obligations of company with respect to articles etc
-- src:12317 | (1) This section applies—
-- src:12318 | (a) to any order under section 899 (order sanctioning compromise or arrangement), and
-- src:12319 | (b) to any order under section 900 (order facilitating reconstruction or amalgamation) that alters the company's constitution.
-- src:12320 | (2) If the order amends—
-- src:12321 | (a) the company's articles, or
-- src:12322 | (b) any resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies (resolution or agreement affecting a company's constitution),
-- src:12323 | the copy of the order delivered to the registrar by the company under section 899(4) or section 900(6) must be accompanied by a copy of the company's articles, or the resolution or agreement in question, as amended.
@ref s 901(1)-(2) Obligations of company with respect to articles etc: the amended articles go with the copy of the order (src:12316-12323)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the copy of the order is delivered to the registrar under section 899(4) or section 900(6); counting="must be accompanied" (the amended articles go with the copy, so they are due on the day of delivery: WITHIN 0)
-- FORK: s 901(2) "must be accompanied" | the amended articles, resolution or agreement are due on the same day as the copy of the order, so the clock is zero days from the day of delivery | a short time after delivery
GIVEN `the order is an order under section 899` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order amends the company's articles or a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 901(2) the company's duty to deliver the amended articles with the copy of the order` MEANS
    IF     (`s 901(1) this section applies to the order` `the order is an order under section 899` `the order is an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the order amends the company's articles or a resolution or agreement to which Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies`
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
         MUST `s 901(2) the company delivers the amended articles, resolution or agreement with the copy of the order`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 895-901 the company` BECAUSE "the copy of the order was delivered to the registrar without the articles, or the resolution or agreement, as amended (s 901(2)): an offence of the company under s 901(5)(a)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:12324 | (3) Every copy of the company's articles issued by the company after the order is made must be accompanied by a copy of the order, unless the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment.
-- src:12328 | (5) If a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:12329 | (a) the company, and
-- src:12330 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 901(3), (5) Every copy of the articles issued after the order; the offence (src:12324-12330)
-- TIMELINE: unit=none; day 0=not applicable; counting=silent (s 901(3) says "every copy ... issued by the company after the order is made" and gives no time, so no clock is encoded and the issue of an unaccompanied copy is an event the trace supplies)
-- FORK: s 901(3) "must be accompanied" | encoded as a prohibition on issuing a copy of the articles without a copy of the order, the company's breach being the offence of s 901(5)(a) | a duty to accompany each copy, breached by a copy issued alone
-- the gate asks the existing s 901(3) function about a copy issued after the order and not accompanied by it: JUST FALSE opens the rule, and JUST TRUE (the effect already incorporated) or NOTHING (s 901 does not apply to the order) closes it
-- not encoded: s 901(5)(b), the officer in default (the company's rule only), as the officer's liability follows the pattern of s 897(5) and s 900(7) above
GIVEN `the order is an order under section 899` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 895-901 party` `ss 895-901 act`
`s 901(3) the company's duty to accompany each copy of the articles with a copy of the order` MEANS
    IF (`s 901(3) the copy of the articles is accompanied as the section requires` (`s 901(1) this section applies to the order` `the order is an order under section 899` `the order is an order under section 900 that alters the company's constitution`) TRUE `the effect of the order has been incorporated into the articles by amendment` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `ss 895-901 the company`
         SHANT `s 901(3) the company issues a copy of the articles unaccompanied by a copy of the order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 895-901 the company` BECAUSE "the company issued a copy of its articles after the order was made without a copy of the order (s 901(3)): an offence under s 901(5)(a)"
    ELSE FULFILLED
